WEBVTT

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.250
<b>Sender: Morioka Moriko 
Recipient: Sakurai Yuta 

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.420
Sh-Sh-She sent a reply!

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.890
Episode 3

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.890
You and I, the Cowards

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.530
Wait a second, Koiwai-san.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.400
That piece isn't cooked, so don't take it yet.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.650
Wha? You're so picky. 
Are you blood type A?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.180
I am.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.320
Seriously? I'm type O.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.280
So I go with the flow, whatever happens.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.610
What does that even matter?

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.040
*Blood types actually have nothing to do with personality

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.420
Anyway, let's get back to the question at hand.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.290
What's up, Sakura-chan?

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.230
Also, why do you call me "Sakura-chan"?

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.680
Man, type A people are real sticklers!

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.050
Don't worry about it. Let's just 
enjoy this all-you-can-eat meat!

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.810
You used to work at Matsukaze Bussan, right?

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.100
You know your stuff.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.180
Nothing less from our 
soon-to-be department head,

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:59.820
full speed ahead on the elite path,
 Sakurai Yuta-kun.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.950
Did you know Morioka Moriko-san? She worked in the distribution

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.830
systems department at Matsukaze Bussan.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.510
Morioka Moriko?

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.210
Oh, you mean Morimori-chan!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.130
Morimori-chan?

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.970
What's up with Morimori-chan?

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.450
Judging by this manual she wrote,

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:22.540
I assumed she was extremely competent
and must be good at her job.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.250
But apparently she resigned.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.160
Morimori-chan was definitely good at her job.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.980
Um, would you mind telling me why 
you keep calling her Morimori-chan?

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.560
It's the nickname I gave her!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.730
How close were you?!

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:41.330
That said, it's not like 
we were friends or anything.

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:44.550
But when I called her 
department at the office,

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.850
she filled in for the person
 in charge sometimes.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:50.880
<i>Excuse me for taking the call. 
My name is Morioka.</i>

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.650
<i>Kawashima isn't available at the moment,</i>

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.790
<i>so if you don't mind,
 I'd be happy to help instead.</i>

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.320
What, really?

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.890
Then could you look over 
some documents for me?

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:01.180
<i>Yes, please send them over. 
I'll tell you when I get them.</i>

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.660
<i>Um, Koiwai-san,</i>

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.060
<i>I'm afraid it will probably take me
 thirty minutes or so to go through them.</i>

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.520
<i>Is that all right?</i>

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.900
I'm fine with that.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.270
Really, Morioka-san,

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.170
I'm sorry for bothering you 
when you're so busy.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.650
You sound really beat.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.030
<i>I-I'm sorry. I was trying my best to hide it.</i>

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.550
I know how you feel. Don't let it get 
to you. Thanks for working so hard.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.580
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.750
Wait, what's wrong? 
You're so tired you're crying?

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.610
<i>No. I'm sorry.</i>

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.990
Don't worry about it.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.800
If you're all alone there, 
then go ahead and cry.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.620
I'm all alone here, too, Mori-chan.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:43.570
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.280
Oh, you don't like being called Mori-chan?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.300
Then what's your given name?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.220
<i>M-Moriko.</i>

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.150
<b>Morioka Moriko</b>

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.060
Mori and Mori?

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.060
<b>Mori    Mori</b>

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.800
So Morimori-chan!

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.190
Something like that.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.800
Whoa...

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.340
Here! This is a picture of Morimori-chan.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.000
Huh?

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.950
<b>Matsukaze 
Bussan
 Systems</b>

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.270
<i>So it really is her!</i>

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.760
She was pretty good-looking.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.440
Wonder what she's up to now.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.900
Maybe I should meet up with her.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.530
Huh?!

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.530
Look, you dropped your 
chopsticks, Sakura-chan.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:40.860
I don't remember raising you 
to be such a vulgar child.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.610
Mom, one fell on the floor. 
Can you pick it up for me?

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:49.030
Come on, it's way more 
on your side than mine.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.620
Where'd the other one go?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.540
It was on the seat.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.750
Gimme that.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.290
Here's a new set.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.630
Thanks.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.050
This is all because you 
didn't hold them properly.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.950
So this is my fault?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.320
I can't believe you talk 
to your elders that way!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:17.340
Sakura-chan, Sakura-chan!

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.040
Which chopsticks did you drop? 
These clean ones? Or these dirty ones?

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:26.400
Koiwai, they both fell on the floor,
so they're both dirty.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.410
Our break's almost over, so please 
just hand me some new chopsticks.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.670
Relax a little, Sakura-chan.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.610
I'm gonna go pick up some coffee.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.050
I'll see you back at the office then.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:08.070
<b>The bruise on my forehead disappeared completely after a couple days.
 Thank you for your concern.
 As for your suggestion to go out to celebrate my recovery,
 when I consider that it was my fault for not watching where I was going
 and that you already paid for my medical treatment,
 I'm afraid I couldn't possibly trouble you any further.</b>

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:07.680
<i>As for your suggestion to go 
out to celebrate my recovery,</i>

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.770
<i>when I consider that it was my fault
 for not watching where I was going,</i>

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.210
<i>and that you already paid 
for my medical treatment,</i>

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.310
<i>I'm afraid I couldn't possibly 
trouble you any further.</i>

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.980
<i>I feel like a lot's happened.</i>

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:41.100
<i>I never thought I'd get an email from a man</i>

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.470
<i>asking to take me out to dinner to apologize.</i>

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.120
Welcome.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:16.350
<i>I thought really hard about how 
to word my reply to Sakurai-san, too.</i>

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:20.810
<i>I did my best to be polite and sincere.</i>

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.310
<i>Right. In my own way.</i>

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:34.950
She looks like she's in a good 
mood for some reason today.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.690
<i>And now I feel completely refreshed.</i>

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.730
Hello.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.030
Hello.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.780
<i>I want to hurry.</i>

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.100
<i>Hurry up and play.</i>

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:33.100
Damn, that's good!

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:41.380
Now I can log in with nothing 
weighing on my mind!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.180
Log in

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.560
There's nothing more refreshing
 than an online game!

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.210
Oh, it's Pokotarou-san.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.150
Hello!

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.960
Oh, Hayashi-kun.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.470
By the look of it, it seems you
 got through what was troubling you.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.880
I heard about it from Li-chan. 
She said you were worried about something.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.220
So the secret's out...

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.680
Well, don't think too badly of her for it.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.980
Everyone's just worried about you.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.380
They're afraid you'll stop logging in

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.320
because you're so preoccupied 
with things in real life.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.590
Sorry for making you worry.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.510
But I think my relationship with 
games works the other way around,

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.240
or maybe it just doesn't matter.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.300
What do you mean?

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.750
When I've got something on my mind, 
I feel like gaming is my salvation.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:50.620
Right? I get you!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.010
But now that everything's been resolved,

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:55.000
I'm refreshed and ready to play!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.800
So everything's all worked out?

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.300
Yup, thanks! Everything's great.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.060
What a relief!

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:15.190
Looks like you got a present.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>New message</b>

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>You've received a present from Lily-san</b>

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>Accept</b>

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>Close</b>

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:21.410
I've received a present from Lily-san?

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.450
Wha?! From Lily-san?!

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.960
This looks expensive.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.960
Can I really accept this?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.960
If I do, I have to give 
her something as thanks.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.470
I feel like I owe her big now.

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:47.510
<b>Crafting</b>

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:49.480
<b>Spell Scrolls</b>

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:49.480
<b>in inventory</b>

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:48.570
Yeah, I can see how that'd 
make you feel as a man.

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:49.480
Right?

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:56.570
Normally it should be the guy 
who's on the ball with this stuff.

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:01.850
I come bearing a brilliant 
ten billion karat gem.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.100
H-Hayashi-san!

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.170
I'd like you to have it

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.200
as a sign of my devotion.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.290
That's how a man should
 treat a lady. Am I right?

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.870
What's up with your image of masculinity?

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.630
Wait, it's starting to influence me now!

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.130
Why should I do?

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.090
Even if I wanted to thank her...

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:27.090
Lily-san can already buy something 
that costs this many points.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:29.180
She must have quite a bit of money.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.680
If I tried to give her something in return,

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.160
she'd probably already have it.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.640
Yeah, that sort of thing can happen.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.440
I know the feeling. That happened 
to me when I first started too.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:47.450
You know our guildmate Nico?

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:57.130
<b>I only give to people I want to cheer on!</b>

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.340
Oh yeah, Nico-san.

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:53.040
I don't really know her, but we've
 done a couple of quests together.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.130
Yeah. She gave me an amazing 
weapon out of nowhere once.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.750
I can see how you'd be 
a bit taken aback by that.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.130
Right? I don't like feeling indebted 
to other people, either.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.100
I was actually pretty upset about it.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:07.640
Yeah?

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:12.640
She told me it was just a prior 
investment, and I ended up taking it.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.640
A prior investment?

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.120
Yeah.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.190
No one loses here.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:22.040
You can just thank me 
with your attitude, Pokotarou.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:25.380
So, well, I guess that's where it all started.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:28.950
She'd always help me out, and I'd always 
try to thank her in my own way.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:28.950
<b>Spell Scroll</b>

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.950
<b>in inventory</b>

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.950
<b>Crafting</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.830
And the reason that's continued

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:34.580
is because, when all's said and done,
 Nico just wants to cheer me on.

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:38.040
I'm sure Lily-chan's the same way.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.840
<b>Crafting</b>

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.840
<b>Spell Scroll</b>

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.840
in inventory

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:40.840
There, all done.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.840
So what are these things you've been making?

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.090
Oh, they're spell scrolls.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:49.780
You normally need a staff to cast spells,

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:53.350
but if you put the magic 
into a scroll, anyone can use it.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.770
Anyway, Hayashi-kun, I'd suggest not 
thinking too hard about that gift.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:03.280
It's probably fine just to keep whatever 
ulterior motives Lily-chan might have in mind.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.230
I see.

00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.360
Huh?

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.490
U-Ulterior motives?!

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.370
What ulterior motives could she have?

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.860
Lily-san's ulterior motives?

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:38.690
This is bad. I keep thinking about it!

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.030
Lily-san!

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.230
I thought you'd be here.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:56.080
Yup. I was just thinking through some things.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.350
Um, thanks a lot for giving me this.

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:17.730
No, no. I guess maybe it 
didn't suit your tastes?

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:20.230
That's not it! Um...

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.190
How should I broach the subject?

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:33.780
I was just wondering if you had some kind 
of ulterior motive in giving me this.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.160
U-Ulterior motive?!

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.290
I just came right out and said it!

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:43.860
Sorry! I mean, I was just thinking 
that I'd feel bad if you did because

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.670
there's nothing I can give you in return.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.300
B-But ulterior motives? Come on!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:52.300
Um, well, I just thought maybe... you know?

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.050
But it's not like that, huh...

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:56.350
<i>He looks disappointed.</i>

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:01.060
I can't say I have absolutely none.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:02.660
<i>So you do?</i>

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:09.130
Hayashi-san, can I tell 
you a bit about myself?

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:10.440
Yeah, of course.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.990
I'd like to hear it. I'm all ears.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.990
Back when I first started playing this game,

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:18.990
<b>Lily-san has logged in.</b>

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:23.250
I used to get quite a few requests 
to go hunting with people every day.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.500
<b>Oh, it's Lily-san.</b>

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.000
<b>It's Lily-san!</b>

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.370
<b>Good evening.</b>

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:22.000
<b>Shi-san</b> has invited you to a party.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.080
<b>Rinarina-san</b> has invited you to a party.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.080
<b>Torippi-san</b> has invited you to a party.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:22.870
<b>riden-san</b> has invited you to a party.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.290
<b>Nice to meet you!</b>

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:26.040
<b>Join my party!</b>

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:26.790
<b>Hey, hey!
My waifu!
You're so cute, Lily-san!</b>

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.250
<b>Hey, hey!
Lily-san!!
Lily-chan!!!</b>

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:36.320
Up until then, all my parties had been PUGs,

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.890
Hey, Lily-san.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:35.800
Hey, Lily-san.

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:40.140
<b>A pick-up group, or PUG, is a party formed when a group of strangers
 get together because they have the same goal.</b>

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:36.960
H-Hello.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:40.440
so part of it was because I was just always 
grouping up with random people.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:37.640
Hello ^^

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:39.100
That last group was fun. 
Let's do it again.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.210
That last group was fun. Let's do it again.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:40.540
Thanks!

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.810
Thanks~ ^^

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:45.020
But once I entered a guild, 
I got to know quite a few people,

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:45.400
Lily-san!

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:48.270
Lily-san

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:43.520
Lily-san

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:43.770
Hello

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:48.270
Why didn't you say something?

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:48.270
There she is!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.350
It's been a while

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.270
and I started getting even more whispers.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.610
Hello!!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:48.270
What are you doing out here all alone?

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:52.780
<b>Popularity of a support role</b>

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.460
And eventually...

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:58.460
What's your relationship with our leader?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:02.040
Uh... Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.040
Don't get any closer to him.

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:15.030
I never knew you went through that.

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.550
It was all a misunderstanding, of course.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.670
Even though we're all online,

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:24.030
it's still pretty difficult to 
handle social relationships.

00:17:24.030 --> 00:17:24.560
Yeah.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:27.940
I kept having that kind of trouble.

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.940
It would have been easy to just quit,

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:35.280
but I really wanted to keep playing.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.490
Why is that?

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:44.080
I met someone really precious 
to me in a game I used to play.

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:49.410
I don't get to see them anymore,

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.850
but I kept thinking 
how wonderful it would be

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:54.650
if I could meet someone else like that.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.090
I'm the same.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.470
You are?

00:17:59.070 --> 00:17:59.970
Yes.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:05.230
I used to play a game with someone 
who always gave me courage.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:14.670
So I completely understand how you feel.

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:18.610
Right. And that's why, even when it was hard,

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:21.450
I wanted to keep playing this game.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:26.290
And then Kanbe-san came along 
and gave me some advice.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:31.270
I see. Well, given how you look, 
it's no surprise you're so popular.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.920
But I just want to have fun and play
 the game like everyone else.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:38.410
Then why don't you try being so over 
the top that everyone doubts your gender?

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:42.430
"I love pink, frills, flowers, 
strawberries, forests,

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.270
and little squirrels frolicking!"

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.060
Or something.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:50.190
If I ever act that obnoxious, 
I'm sure I'd lose <i>all</i> of my friends.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.310
No dice? Then...

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.690
I know! Just say you're my partner.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.380
Partner?

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.200
It'll just be on paper.

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:04.200
But if you say you're my partner, 
I don't think anyone'll give you a hard time.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.080
But is that really okay?

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.460
Sure. Why not?

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:11.710
Thank you!

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.820
That's why I've always been a bit scared

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:24.270
to get too close with anyone in game.

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:25.900
I guess you could say I was on my guard.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:30.850
But then I met you.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.110
Watching you,

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:37.330
I felt like you really enjoyed
 playing this game.

00:19:37.330 --> 00:19:40.990
It made me enjoy the game more myself.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:45.740
Hayashi-san.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:46.990
Y-Yes?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.000
Would you...

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:54.500
What? Lily-san, what are 
you trying to tell me?

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.730
...become my partner?

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:06.760
Partner?!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:08.270
Lily-san!

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:13.590
My main is a support class, so I end up 
grouping with a lot of different people,

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:16.770
but I've really enjoyed 
grouping up with you lately.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.650
You... have?

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.560
I have all sorts of reasons,

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.160
but just to put it simply...

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:28.910
I feel most at peace when 
playing together with you.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:33.670
This is bad! Really bad!

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.020
My heart won't stop racing!

00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:36.440
I'm overjoyed!

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:39.170
So much so that the word "overjoyed" 
doesn't even do it justice!

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.170
It's been a while since 
I've felt this excited.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:46.710
Is this what they call having a crush, or...

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:47.300
Come on!

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.810
How could I be thinking 
like this in my thirties?!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.580
<i>She's even a girl! I'm sure there's 
nothing romantic going on here!</i>

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.690
<i>And first and foremost, 
she's someone I only know online!</i>

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:58.520
<i>But...</i>

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:03.770
<i>I'm just so happy.</i>

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:05.990
Lily-san.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:06.700
Yes?

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:10.700
How do I look?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.710
It looks great on you.

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.710
Thanks a lot.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.480
Hayashi-san, um... Does this mean...?

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:24.300
Yes. I'm looking forward to being 
your partner from now on.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:30.940
So she really did have an ulterior motive.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.780
Look at how stupidly happy those two 
MMO junkies are! Damn, I'm jealous!

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:37.860
I'm glad you found someone you 
get along so well with, Lily.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:44.950
Lily-san!

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:54.960
Lily:  Hayashi-san, um... Does this mean...? 
Hayashi:  Yes. I'm looking forward to being your partner 
Hayashi:  from now on! 
Lily:  I feel the same way, Hayashi-san!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:40.100
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.330 --> 00:23:27.590
Once you know, it's all over.

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:28.520
Please stop!

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:30.370
She said she'd go out on a date with me.

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:31.470
No way.

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:34.970
As soon as you want something, 
it slips out of reach.

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.510
Episode 4, "Like a Maiden in Love."

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:40.180
<b>Episode 4 
Like a Maiden in Love</b>
